BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iffr-darkroom-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T203516Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Darkroom 2027: Work-in-Progress Showcase (IFFR Pro)
DESCRIPTION:Darkroom is IFFR's work-in-progress platform\, running during C
 ineMart\, where recently completed or nearly finished films are launched t
 o the international film industry. Selected teams present an excerpt of th
 eir work to international sales agents\, festival programmers\, buyers and
  other industry professionals in a closed presentation\, and receive tailo
 red mentorship matched to the project's needs from senior editors\, market
 ing strategists\, festival experts and distribution professionals. All Dar
 kroom projects get a curated agenda of one-to-one meetings with potential 
 creative and business partners plus facilitated informal networking\, and 
 IFFR Pro awards are handed out to projects from the selection. ELIGIBILITY
 : the project must have been supported by IFFR through at least one of the
  following: new for 2027\, the filmmaker has been selected for the Tiger C
 ompetition or Bright Future programme at IFFR within the last 10 years\; t
 he project has been supported by the Hubert Bals Fund through any of its f
 unding schemes\; the project was formerly presented at BoostNL\; the proje
 ct was formerly presented at CineMart\; or the project's main producer or 
 main co-producer has been a Rotterdam Lab participant. In addition\, the p
 roject must have no sales agent attached\, Darkroom must be its first work
 -in-progress showcase\, and it must not have a confirmed world or internat
 ional premiere at the time of application (if that changes after selection
  at a winter festival\, applicants must tell the Darkroom team immediately
  so eligibility can be rechecked). Projects that do not meet all criteria 
 are ineligible. Recent editions selected 6 to 12 projects. Deadline 1 Octo
 ber 2026\, 22:00 UTC. Free to submit.\n\nOrganisation: International Film 
 Festival Rotterdam (IFFR)\nLocation: Rotterdam\, Netherlands. Presentation
 s take place during CineMart at IFFR 2027 (28 January to 7 February 2027).
  Open internationally: eligibility is defined by the project's prior conne
 ction to IFFR\, not by the applicant's country.\nAward: No participation f
 ee and no fee to submit. Selected projects compete for the IFFR Pro awards
  attached to Darkroom: the Eurimages Outreach Award of EUR 30\,000 (shared
  with Lightroom)\, the HBF Empowerment Award of EUR 10\,000\, the Filmmore
  Work-in-progress Post-production Award of EUR 5\,000\, and the 4DR Studio
 s Award (an in-kind studio or workshop prize\, shared with CineMart). Part
 icipation also includes tailored mentorship\, a closed industry presentati
 on and a curated agenda of one-to-one meetings. Award line-up is per the m
 ost recent published edition and may change for 2027.\nDuration: Work-in-p
 rogress showcase during CineMart at IFFR 2027\, 28 January to 7 February 2
 027\n\nMore: https://iffr.com/en/iffr-pro/darkroom?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://iffr.com/en/iffr-pro/darkroom?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rotterdam\, Netherlands. Presentations take place during CineMart 
 at IFFR 2027 (28 January to 7 February 2027). Open internationally: eligib
 ility is defined by the project's prior connection to IFFR\, not by the ap
 plicant's country.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:next-art-ai-award-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T203516Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI ART AWARD: NEXT ART AI 2026
DESCRIPTION:NEXT ART AI is an open AI art competition run by the HOBAN Cult
 ural Foundation\, welcoming participants of all backgrounds regardless of 
 career\, nationality or age\, and framed as a way to reflect on the future
  of AI art through new modes of expression and artistic experimentation. T
 WO CATEGORIES: AI IMAGE ART\, for works in a single-image format at 150dpi
  or higher\, submitted as JPG\, JPEG\, PNG or BMP up to 10MB\; and AI VIDE
 O ART\, open to a wide range of video formats including animation\, motion
  graphics and live-action footage enhanced or transformed using AI\, at 10
 80p or higher\, under one minute\, 30 or 60fps recommended\, stereo 48kHz 
 audio recommended\, as mp4 (h.264) or mov. Video entries are submitted as 
 a URL via YouTube\, Vimeo\, Dropbox or OneDrive\, or an alternative platfo
 rm if those are restricted in your region\; links that are inaccessible du
 e to privacy settings may be excluded from judging. WHO CAN ENTER: individ
 uals or teams of up to three including the representative\, though you may
  not submit both as an individual and as part of a team. Team representati
 ves create the account in their own name and all members submit a consent 
 form for personal data. Applicants under 19 need a guardian's signed conse
 nt. One work may be submitted per category. RULES ON AI AND ASSETS: work m
 ust be original and created by the applicant or team\, and must be image o
 r video art created using generative AI platforms. Works that have previou
 sly won an award in another competition are not eligible. Free or paid ext
 ernal assets\, game engines\, AI frameworks\, open-source tools and editin
 g software may be used freely\, but applicants must hold licences permitti
 ng commercial use for every element\, and work infringing third-party righ
 ts is excluded. Even where external assets and editing software are used\,
  the creative process must involve AI\, whether AI-assisted direction\, tr
 ansformation\, generation or other AI-based processes\, and the choice of 
 AI tools\, the scope and method of their use\, and the prompts themselves 
 are all weighed in evaluating the creative use of AI. TIMELINE: applicatio
 ns open 1 September 2026 and close 30 September 2026 at 11:59pm KST\, prel
 iminary round early October\, final round late October\, announcement and 
 ceremony early November\, exhibition late November 2026. Organised and hos
 ted by the HOBAN Cultural Foundation\, sponsored by HOBAN Group\, with Seo
 ul Shinmun and EBN as media partners. Details and schedule are subject to 
 change at the organiser's discretion.\n\nOrganisation: HOBAN Cultural Foun
 dation\nLocation: Online submission\, with the awards ceremony and exhibit
 ion in South Korea. Open to all regardless of career\, nationality or age.
 \nAward: Total prize pool of KRW 21\,000\,000 across 20 winners\, paid aft
 er deduction of applicable taxes and public charges. Grand Prize KRW 5\,00
 0\,000 (selected regardless of category)\; in each of the two categories\,
  First Prize KRW 2\,000\,000\, three Second Prizes of KRW 1\,000\,000 each
 \, and five Honorable Finalist awards of KRW 500\,000 each\; plus a HOBAN 
 Group President's Award of KRW 1\,000\,000. Winners also receive plaques a
 nd certificates\, online and offline exhibition opportunities\, and a feat
 ure on the official online platform. No entry fee is mentioned.\nDuration:
  One-off competition\; exhibition late November 2026\n\nMore: https://next
 -art-ai.com/en/apply/overview?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://next-art-ai.com/en/apply/overview?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online submission\, with the awards ceremony and exhibition in Sou
 th Korea. Open to all regardless of career\, nationality or age.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:epic-megagrants-cycle-2-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T203516Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:Deadline: Epic MegaGrants 2026 (Cycle 2)
DESCRIPTION:Epic MegaGrants are financial grants from Epic Games for creati
 ve\, noteworthy and innovative projects built in and around Unreal Engine\
 , or projects that enhance the open source 3D graphics ecosystem. Over 2\,
 000 grants have been awarded to date. The programme is explicitly aimed at
  smaller teams\, solo developers and individuals as well as studios: Epic 
 states that individuals and small teams are eligible and encouraged\, and 
 that it treats every project equally regardless of who you are. WHAT IS FU
 NDED: (1) INDIE GAMES\, small or solo teams working in Unreal Engine\, sub
 mitted past the idea and design phase with at least some working prototype
 \, ideally with a video link\; (2) UEFN EXPERIENCES\, Fortnite Creative is
 lands and interactive experiences built in Unreal Editor for Fortnite\; (3
 ) ENGINE MIGRATION\, a proportion of MegaGrants is reserved for teams movi
 ng a partially developed project from another engine to Unreal\; (4) FILM\
 , TV AND LIVE EVENTS\, including live-action and animated films and shows\
 , broadcast\, live and location-based events\; (5) OTHER NON-GAMES VERTICA
 LS such as architecture\, automotive\, manufacturing\, simulation\, produc
 t design\, advertising and VR/AR\, where more detailed project plans and p
 rototypes are expected\; (6) EDUCATION\, including research\, curricula an
 d course development and university programmes\, though for institutions E
 pic accepts submissions only from degree-granting schools and educators at
  such schools\; (7) TOOLS AND OPEN SOURCE\, creating open source tools or 
 enhancing open source software using Unreal Engine. NON-UNREAL PROJECTS AR
 E ELIGIBLE if you want to move them to Unreal Engine\, or if the project e
 nhances open source 3D content creation whether or not it relates to Unrea
 l Engine. EVALUATION rests on three things: quality and unique appeal (hig
 h-quality demos or builds\, well-documented descriptions\, technical ambit
 ion)\; community benefit (how you will give back\, for example open-sourci
 ng the project\, releasing assets through a marketplace\, sharing learning
 s\, or shipping an SDK\, tool or plug-in)\; and viability (a clear budget 
 with major spend areas and a project plan with milestones\, deliverables a
 nd timeline). NOTE ON DEADLINES: the FAQ still describes MegaGrants as an 
 ongoing programme with no specific deadline\, but the timeline published o
 n the same page now runs in fixed cycles\, and the Cycle 2 submission wind
 ow closes 4 September 2026 at 23:59 ET. Treat the cycle date as the operat
 ive deadline. You may apply for more than one project\, and may reapply fo
 r the same project after a decision if you have made updates. Epic is not 
 offering sponsorships and cannot give feedback on applications. Apply at m
 egagrants.unrealengine.com.\n\nOrganisation: Epic Games\nLocation: Open wo
 rldwide. Epic states that if it can legally make payment to you\, you are 
 eligible.\nAward: Typical grants range from USD 5\,000 to USD 75\,000\, wi
 th some exceptional projects receiving up to USD 150\,000. Epic states tha
 t recipients continue to own their IP and may publish it however they wish
 \, so this is a grant rather than an investment or equity deal. Grants up 
 to and including USD 25\,000 may be paid in a single instalment\; larger g
 rants are paid across several instalments tied to continued progress. Fund
 s are for project and team expenses such as development and hiring\; hardw
 are purchases or rentals are approved only occasionally\, case by case. No
  application fee.\nDuration: Cycle 2 of 2026 runs 29 June to 11 December 2
 026. Submission window 29 June to 4 September 2026 (closes 23:59 ET)\, rev
 iew 5 September to 4 December 2026\, notices 7 to 11 December 2026. Cycle 
 1 ran 12 January to 19 June 2026.\n\nMore: https://www.unrealengine.com/me
 gagrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.unrealengine.com/megagrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open worldwide. Epic states that if it can legally make payment to
  you\, you are eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:frameline-completion-fund-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T203516Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261010
SUMMARY:Deadline: Frameline Completion Fund 2027
DESCRIPTION:Long-running post-production grant from Frameline\, the San Fra
 ncisco organisation behind the world's longest-running LGBTQ+ film festiva
 l\, for films that represent and reflect LGBTQ+ life in all its complexity
  and richness. Grants run up to USD 5\,000\, typically USD 1\,000 to 5\,00
 0\, and the jury may recommend more or less than that range. WHAT IT COVER
 S: any post-production cost\, explicitly including editing\, special effec
 ts and graphics\, music licensing\, photo licensing\, and\, notably\, clos
 ed captioning and audio description\, so accessibility work is fundable ra
 ther than an afterthought. STAGE GATE\, the thing that disqualifies most a
 pplicants: your project must be at least 90 percent complete with a rough 
 cut available\, and in or about to enter post-production. Work still in de
 velopment or mid-production is not eligible. WHO AND WHAT: all formats\, l
 engths\, genres and nationalities are welcome\, spanning documentary\, nar
 rative\, experimental\, animated and episodic work\, so long as the film i
 s about LGBTQ+ people and their communities. Directors must have creative 
 and financial control of the project. NO APPLICATION FEE\, which is worth 
 flagging given how many completion funds charge one. TIMING: the submissio
 n window opens 31 August 2026 and closes 9 October 2026\, with decisions i
 n January 2027. The 2026 cycle's grantees have already been announced ahea
 d of Frameline's 50th festival\, so this is the next round.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Frameline\nLocation: Administered from San Francisco\, United States. O
 pen to filmmakers of all nationalities.\nAward: Grants of up to USD 5\,000
 \, with a standard range of USD 1\,000 to 5\,000\; the jury can recommend 
 amounts above or below that range. No application fee.\nDuration: Submissi
 on window opens 31 August 2026 and closes 9 October 2026\, with notificati
 on in January 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.frameline.org/artist-development/
 completion-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.frameline.org/artist-development/completion-fund?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Administered from San Francisco\, United States. Open to filmmaker
 s of all nationalities.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
